00\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0013 SEQ CHAPTER \\h \\r 1\u0015MINUTES OF A REGULAR MEETING OF\rTHE CITY COUNCIL OF THE CITY OF CALABASAS,\rCALIFORNIA, HELD WEDNESDAY, APRIL 14, 2010\r\rMayor Groveman called the meeting to order at 6:00 p.m. in the Closed Session Conference Room, 100 Civic Center Way, Calabasas, California.\r\rROLL CALL Present: Mayor Groveman, Mayor pro Tem Washburn, Councilmembers Bozajian, Maurer, Wolfson.\r Absent: None.\r Staff: Colantuono, Coroalles.\r\rCLOSED SESSION\r\rThe City Council recessed at 6:01 p.m. into closed session to confer with legal counsel regarding the following:\r\rInitiation of Litigation, pursuant to Government Code Section 54956.9(c): two cases.\r\rThe City Council reconvened at 6:55 p.m. from closed session, and Mayor Groveman called the meeting to order at 7:05 p.m. in the City Council Chambers of City Hall, 100 Civic Center Way, Calabasas, California.\r\rROLL CALL Present: Mayor Groveman, Mayor pro Tem Washburn, Councilmembers Bozajian, Maurer, Wolfson.\r Absent: None.\r Staff: Colantuono, Coroalles, Peirce, Tamuri, Yalda.\r\rThe Pledge of Allegiance was led by Gary Klein.\r\rMichael G. Colantuono, City Attorney, City Attorney, reported that the City Council authorized him to file a proceeding in regards to the dispute with Calabasas Park Homeowners Association and access to the lake.\r\rAPPROVAL OF AGENDA\r\r Councilmember Wolfson moved, seconded by Councilmember Maurer, to approve the agenda. MOTION CARRIED 5/0. \r\rANNOUNCEMENTS/INTRODUCTIONS \r\r Mayor pro Tem Washburn announced that the meeting will be adjourned in memory of Susan Ann Boething. Councilmember Maurer spoke regarding residents returning their Census 2010 forms. Councilmember Maurer announced the upcoming Santa Monica Mountains Science Festival that will be happening at Paramount Ranch on April 16 and 17 and the Nuts for Mutts 5K Walk that will be occurring on April 18 at the Community Center. Councilmember Bozajian announced that the Calabasas Fine Arts Festival and the Friends of the Calabasas Library Book Sale will both be held on May 1 and 2, 2010. Mayor pro Tem Washburn spoke regarding the upcoming Anza en Calabasas Historical Pageant that will be taking place on April 24.\r\rORAL COMMUNICATIONS - PUBLIC COMMENT\r\r Kimberly Bordonaro, Calabasas Chamber of Commerce, presented the annual Book of Accomplishments, highlighting the Calabasas Chamber�s programs that benefit the community. Dale Reicheneder, Calabasas, representing Steeplechase Homeowners Association, spoke in opposition to the proposed aquatic center at De Anza Park.\r\r\rCONSENT ITEMS\r \r Approval of meeting minutes from March 10, 2010 and March 24, 2010.\r\r Introduction of Ordinance No. 2010-273, revising the Purchasing Guidelines, Section 3.40 of the Calabasas Municipal Code to delete requirement for City to maintain a bidder list.\r\r Recommendation to approve City budget adjustment and authorize expenditure for the Volvo frontage street improvements project.\r\r Adoption of Resolution No. 2010-1230, executing the Program Supplement Agreement No. N015 to administering Agency-State Agreement No. 07-5463r to fund AE Wright School Pedestrian Footbridge and Trail Project.\r\r Recommendation to accept completion for the 2009 Annual Rubberized Overlay Project, Specification No. 08-09-04, by Silvia Construction, Inc., and to direct the City Clerk to file notice of completion.\r\r Adoption of Resolution of No. 2010-1231, approving the 16th Cycle Used Oil Recycling Block Grant, Fiscal Year 2010-2011.\r\r Adoption of Resolution No. 2010-1232, approving applications for grant funds for the Urban Greening Grant Program under the Safe Drinking Water, Water Quality and Supply, Flood Control, River and Coastal Protection Bon Act of 2006 (Proposition 84).\r\r Notice of Completion for the Las Virgenes and Agoura Road Bus Shelter project, specification number 08-09-03.\r\r Authorization to approve an amendment to extend the professional services agreement with Arch Chemicals, Inc., also known as Marine Biochemists of California, and approve budgeted funding to cover the annual cost of maintaining Calabasas Lake and repair or replacement of lake aeration equipment.\r\r Adoption of Resolution No. 2010-1235, amending Resolution No. 2009-1190 by approving the position of an hourly part-time Assistant Landscape Manager.\r\r Recommendation to approve the reappointment of Ellen Pangarliotas by Mayor Groveman and David Shapiro by Councilmember Wolfson to the Library Commission, terms ending March 31, 2013.\r\rCouncilmember Wolfson moved, seconded by Mayor pro Tem Washburn, to approve Consent Items #1, 3, 5, 6, 8, 9, and 10. MOTION CARRIED 5/0. Councilmember Wolfson noted his ABSTENTION on Item #9.\r\rMayor Groveman moved, seconded by Councilmember Wolfson, to approve Consent Item #11. MOTION CARRIED 5/0.\r\rCouncilmember Maurer moved, seconded by Mayor pro Tem Washburn, to approve Consent Item #2. MOTION CARRIED 5/0.\r\rFollowing discussion, Councilmember Bozajian moved, seconded by Councilmember Maurer to approve Consent Item #4. MOTION CARRIED 5/0.\r\rFollowing discussion, Mayor pro Tem Washburn moved, seconded by Councilmember Bozajian to approve Consent Item #7. MOTION CARRIED 5/0.\r\rSPECIAL ITEM\r\r Presentation by Deputy Mark Merino of Malibu/Lost Hills Sheriff�s Station on School Resource Deputy activities.\r\rThis item was continued to a future City Council meeting.\rNEW BUSINESS\r\r Discussion regarding funding maintenance of Lake Calabasas from 1911 Act Assessment proceeds.\r\rCouncilmember Wolfson recused himself and left the room due to the proximity of his residence to the area being discussed.\r\rCity Manager Coroalles and City Attorney Colantuono presented background information on the staff report.\r\rDan Scully, Director, Calabasas Park Homeowners Association (CPHA), Jeff Cooper, Executive Boardmember, CPHA, David Litt, CPHA, Barry Hammond, CPHA, Harold Arkoff, Calabasas, Helene Regen, CPHA, Glen Kulick, Attorney representing CPHA, provided background information on the agreement between the City and CPHA and spoke in support of the City�s continued maintenance of Lake Calabasas and if individuals would like to have access, then they should become members of CPHA. Victor Kenton, Calabasas, Gary Klein, representing the Calabasas Hills Homeowners Association, Kathy Berman, CPHA, spoke in support of the City ensuring that all Landscape Maintenance District 22 taxpayers are allowed to have access to Lake Calabasas and not just members of CPHA. Donald Low, Calabasas, Brian Cameron, Calabasas, Temah Volen, Calabasas, Gail Schroeder, Calabasas, spoke in support of the City continuing to maintain Lake Calabasas and allowing only members of CPHA to have access to the lake. \r\rCouncilmember Bozajian moved, seconded by Mayor pro Tem Washburn, to direct the City Manager and City Attorney to prepare some form of dispute resolution, such as a declaratory relief action, that can produce a legally binding judgment on the question whether 1911 Act funds can be used for lake maintenance without making lake access available to all residents of the 1911 Act district.� Additional Council action is required before that dispute resolution process may be initiated. MOTION CARRIED 4/0. Councilmember Wolfson was recused.\r\rThe City Council recessed at 9:15 p.m. and reconvened at 9:30 p.m.\r\r Adoption of Resolution No. 2010-1234, granting a request from Mehdi and Betty Ahmadi for a one-year permit extension of Conditional Use Permit No. 700-002 and Oak Tree Permit No. 007-002, to construct a new single-family residence located at 24226 Dry Canyon Cold Creek Road, in accordance with the provisions of Ordinance No. 2009-260.\r\rMayor pro Tem Washburn moved, seconded by Councilmember Bozajian, to adopt Resolution 2010-1234, granting a request from Mehdi and Betty Ahmadi for a one-year permit extension of Conditional Use Permit No. 700-002 and Oak Tree Permit No. 007-002, to construct a new single-family residence located at 24226 Dry Canyon Cold Creek Road, in accordance with the provisions of Ordinance No. 2009-260. MOTION CARRIED 5/0.\r\rPUBLIC HEARING\r\r Motion to waive further reading and introduction of Ordinance No. 2010-272, amending Titles 5 and 17 of the Calabasas Municipal Code to prohibit the sale of tobacco products within 500 feet of schools located in the City of Calabasas.\r\rMayor Groveman opened the public hearing.\r\rNo one indicated a desire to speak.\r\rMayor Groveman closed the public hearing.\r\rCouncilmember Wolfson moved, seconded by Mayor pro Tem Washburn, to waive further reading and introduce Ordinance No. 2010-272, amending Titles 5 and 17 of the Calabasas Municipal Code to prohibit the sale of tobacco products within 500 feet of schools located in the City of Calabasas. MOTION CARRIED 5/0.\r\r Adoption of Resolution 2010-1233, establishing Public Works fees on an interim basis pending Resolution 2010-1227 becoming effective.\r\rMayor Groveman opened the public hearing.\r\rNo one indicated a desire to speak.\r\rMayor Groveman closed the public hearing.\r\rMayor pro Tem Washburn moved, seconded by Councilmember Wolfson, to adopt Resolution 2010-1233, establishing Public Works fees on an interim basis pending Resolution 2010-1227 becoming effective. MOTION CARRIED 5/0.\r\rUNFINISHED BUSINESS \r\r Continued discussion regarding ethical guidelines for Commissioners and a Commissioner removal ordinance.\r\rCouncilmember Wolfson moved, seconded Councilmember Maurer, to waive further reading and introduce Ordinance No. 2010-274 with revisions. MOTION CARRIED 5/0.\r\rCouncilmember Wolfson moved, seconded by Councilmember Maurer, to approve the ethical guidelines for commissioners. MOTION CARRIED 5/0.\r\rINFORMATIONAL REPORTS \r\r Check Register for the period of March 4, 2010 to April 1, 2010.\r\rThere was no action taken.\r\rTASK FORCE REPORTS \r\r Councilmember Maurer and Mayor pro Tem Washburn provided information on a recent Headwaters Corners Master Plan meeting.\r\rCITY MANAGER�S REPORT \r\r City Manager Coroalles indicated he had nothing to report\r\rFUTURE AGENDA ITEMS \r\r Councilmember Wolfson requested that recognition of student commissioners be placed on the agenda for May 26.\r\r\u0013 SEQ CHAPTER \\h \\r 1\u0015ADJOURN \r\rThe City Council adjourned at 10:07 p.m. in memory of Susan Ann Boething to their next regular meeting, which will be held on Wednesday, April 28, 2010 at 7:00 p.m.\r\r\r\r\r\r__________________________\rGwen Peirce, CMC, City Clerk\r\r\u0003\r\r\u0004\r\r\u0003\r\r\u0004\r\r\u0013 PAGE \\* MERGEFORMAT \u00142\u0015\r\r\r\u0013 PAGE \\* MERGEFORMAT \u00144\u0015\r\r\r\r\r\r\r\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u